.TH CSYC 1 "" "csyc" "CSy compiler"
.SH NAME
csyc \- the CSy compiler and runner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B csyc
.I file.csy
.RI [ files... ]
.RB [ \-\- " args..." ]
.br
.B csyc build
.RI [ project.csp | file.csy ]
.RB [ \-o " out.cso"]
.br
.B csyc run
.I file.cso
.br
.B csyc init
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B csyc install
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-prefix " DIR]"
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-deps ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B csyc doctor
.RB [ \-\-prefix " DIR]"
.br
.B csyc explain
.RI [ NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-path " file.csy|project.csp]"
.br
.B csyc enable ccm
|
.B csyc disable ccm
.br
.B csyc wipe \-\-ccm\-mem
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.br
.B csyc \-\-help
|
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B csyc
compiles CSy programs to bytecode (with an optional native fast path) and runs them.
A project is described by a
.B project.csp
file; a single source file needs no project.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I file.csy
Compile and run. A
.I project.csp
or a
.I file.cso
may be given instead, and
.B csyc .
compiles ./main.csy.
.TP
.B build
Compile without running. With no argument it builds ./project.csp. The object is written next to the entry file unless
.B \-o
or the project's
.B output
says otherwise.
.TP
.B run
Run a compiled object, rebuilding it first from the matching source or project when that is newer.
.TP
.BI init " [path]"
Create a default project in
.I path
(default: the current folder; missing folders are created):
.BR project.csp ,
.B src/main.csy
,
.B .gitignore
and a copy of the Cooler Compiler table
.BR ccm_table.bin .
Existing files are never overwritten, and a folder that already has a project.csp is refused.
.TP
.B install
Detect the operating system (Linux distributions; Windows and macOS are refused for now), offer to add the optional C compiler with the
system package manager (apt\-get, dnf or yum, pacman, zypper, apk, xbps\-install), then copy this csyc to
.IR DIR /bin/csyc
(default prefix /usr). Steps that need administrator rights run through sudo or doas, which ask for your password.
If a csyc is already there it stops;
.B \-\-force
replaces it. The binary and the Cooler Compiler table (DIR/share/csyc/ccm_table.bin, never replacing an existing one unless
.B \-\-force
is given) are installed; the packages also add this manual page and the docs.
.TP
.B doctor
Show the detected operating system, the package manager, the administrator rights available, whether a C compiler is present,
and the state of the install target, without changing anything.
.TP
.BI explain " [NAME] [\-\-path file]"
Print what the
.B #explain
lines of a CSy file say about a function or variable: the text, the line where it is declared, and the names it refers to.
.I NAME
may be
.I namespace::name
for something in a connected file. Without a name every function and variable of the file is listed.
.B \-\-path
takes a .csy file or a project.csp (all of the project's files are then searched); without it ./project.csp is used.
.TP
.B enable ccm, disable ccm
Switch the Cooler Compiler on or off (the key "cooler_compiler" in csyconf.json).
.TP
.B wipe \-\-ccm\-mem
Ask, then wipe the Cooler Compiler memory. Without a terminal it needs
.BR \-\-yes .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
Explain each build stage and show progress.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write a compiled object (for a source build: the object, then run it).
.TP
.B \-\-exe
With build: write a standalone executable (runtime plus program).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-native
Skip the native fast path.
.TP
.B \-\-explain\-native
Report which functions run natively and why the others do not.
.TP
.BI \-\-memory\-limit " MB"
Compiler memory budget (default 2048; 0 disables the limit).
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N|auto"
Cap compiler worker threads (at most 256).
.TP
.BI \-\-run\-threads " N|auto"
Threads for the built-in AI kernels at run time.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With install: replace an installed csyc.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
With install: install the C compiler package without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-deps
With install: do not look at the C compiler at all.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With install: show what would be run and installed, and change nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " DIR"
With install: install under DIR instead of /usr.
.TP
.B \-\-
Everything after it is passed to the program (bc::args()).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B project.csp
Project description: entry, sources, output.
.TP
.B csyconf.json
In the project folder. "cooler_compiler": true turns the Cooler Compiler on; it is off otherwise.
.TP
.B ccm_table.bin
In the project folder. The lines the Cooler Compiler says. It is a data file, not part of the compiler: it is installed in
/usr/share/csyc/ccm_table.bin and csyc init copies it into every new project. To customise it, decode the project's copy
with ccm_tools.py decode, edit the text, run ccm_tools.py encode and put the result back in the project folder.
.TP
.B ccm_mem.bin
In the project folder. What the Cooler Compiler remembers (at most 500 records).
.TP
.B /usr/share/doc/csyc
README, notes, the table template and ccm_tools.py.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CSYC_DATA_DIR
When set, the only folder searched for the shipped ccm_table.bin (otherwise PREFIX/share/csyc next to the binary's folder, the folder
of the binary, /usr/local/share/csyc and /usr/share/csyc).
.TP
.B CSYC_MEMORY_LIMIT_MB, CSYC_THREADS
Defaults for \-\-memory\-limit and \-\-threads.
.TP
.B CC
C compiler for the optional C native backend (the own x86\-64 backend needs none).
.TP
.B CSY_NO_NATIVE_JIT
Set to 1 to disable the native fast path.
.TP
.B CSY_JIT_CACHE_DIR
Where compiled native code is cached (default /tmp/csy_native_jit\-UID).
.TP
.B CSY_PROFILE
Print timing and memory figures.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Gray Cooler Compiler lines are printed without colour codes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a compile error, a runtime error, or a bad command line; otherwise the program's own exit code.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README and notes in /usr/share/doc/csyc.
